## SLM Commander Training Strategy (The Critical Piece)

### Phase 1: Persona + Retrieval (Day 1 — runs immediately)
- System prompt: 25-year NSE veteran persona (full SKILL_nse_specialist.md + SKILL_intraday.md injected)
- RAG over learnings DB: every SLM call gets last 30 relevant learnings fetched by ticker + pattern tags
- Even without fine-tuning, the SLM reasons with accumulated institutional context

### Phase 2: Claude Distillation (Week 3–4 — after data pipeline runs)
Use `claude -p` CLI to generate 10,000+ commander training pairs from 26yr NSE data:

```
Input prompt to Claude:
"You are a 25-year NSE veteran. Given this historical situation:
Ticker: HDFCBANK | Date: 2016-11-09 (day after demonetization)
RSI: 41 | Volume: 4.1x | MACD: negative cross | Price: 12% below 50-DMA
FII: net sellers ₹4200Cr | Sector: Banking | Nifty: -6.5% previous day

What would you have done? Give your full reasoning and decision."

Target output: Structured JSON with decision, stop_loss, target, reasoning,
key_risk_factors, what_to_watch
```

Generate pairs for:
- Every major market event (demonetization, COVID crash, 2008, IL&FS, Yes Bank)
- Each of 50 top NSE stocks across 26yr of signals
- All sector rotation patterns identified in historical data
- Budget days, RBI policy days, expiry weeks
- Result: ~10,000–15,000 training pairs, all generated via Claude CLI (free)

### Phase 3: QLoRA Fine-tune (Week 5–6)
- Framework: Unsloth (designed for sub-8GB VRAM)
- Base: Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct (7B) — fallback to 3B if 7B OOMs during training
- Method: QLoRA 4-bit, LoRA rank=16, target modules: q_proj, v_proj
- Hardware: RTX 3050 4GB — Unsloth confirmed working at this spec
- Expected: 8–12 hours per epoch, 3 epochs = 2–3 days
- Output: LoRA adapter saved, merged with base → deployed via Ollama

### Phase 4: Continuous Improvement (Month 2+)
- Every EOD review adds to learnings DB
- Monthly retrain: add new signal→outcome pairs to training set
- Model improves on YOUR specific signal history — no one else's data

