Full 26-year NSE fine-tuning — no data skipped.

**Why all 26 years matter for Kronos:**
- 2001 dot-com bust (IT stocks collapse)
- 2003–2007 bull run (Sensex 3000 → 21000)
- 2008 Lehman crash (Sensex -60% in months)
- 2009 recovery (fastest V-shape in NSE history)
- 2013 taper tantrum (INR crisis)
- 2016 demonetization (overnight 8% gap down)
- 2018 IL&FS collapse (NBFC sector wipeout)
- 2020 COVID crash + fastest recovery
- 2021 smallcap euphoria
- 2022 FII exodus (rate hike cycle)
- 2024 election volatility

Kronos trained on only recent years would never learn how Indian markets behave in crisis regimes, sector-specific crashes, and policy shock events. All 26 years is mandatory.

**Implementation:**
- Load all NSE daily OHLCV from DB: 1994–2026, all 2000+ stocks
- Format as Kronos training sequences (OHLCV windows, same format as their A-share fine-tune)
- Fine-tune `base` model (102.3M params — fits 4GB VRAM in FP16)
- Use all data: do not filter by date, do not skip any market regime
- Save fine-tuned weights to `models/kronos/weights/nse_26yr_finetuned/`
- Expected training time: 6–12 hours on RTX 3050 (run overnight)
- Inference always uses fine-tuned weights, falls back to base if weights missing

