## Key Design Decisions

1. **Claude CLI, never API**: All `claude` calls via `subprocess.run(["claude", "-p", ...])`. Zero API cost beyond Claude Code subscription. Models: `claude-sonnet-4-5` for intraday batch, `claude-opus-4-5` for EOD/weekend deep review.

2. **SSE not WebSocket**: One-way server push is correct for this use case. Frontend never sends trading commands to backend. Simpler, more reliable.

3. **APScheduler not Celery**: No message broker needed. Single-machine, async, IST timezone-aware. Celery is overkill.

4. **Unsloth for SLM fine-tuning**: Designed specifically for consumer GPUs (3050/4GB). 2x faster than vanilla HuggingFace training, 60% less VRAM. This is the only viable path for local fine-tuning at this hardware spec.

5. **TimescaleDB not plain PostgreSQL**: 26yr of daily data for 2000 stocks = ~150M rows. TimescaleDB hypertable partitioning makes time-range queries 10-100x faster. Already in schema.sql.

6. **TradingView Lightweight Charts not full widget**: Free, open-source, same visual quality as Angel One's charts. Full TradingView widget requires paid plan for custom data.

7. **yfinance first, SmartAPI second**: yfinance covers the 26yr historical requirement. SmartAPI adds real-time 1-min ticks. Historical data is more valuable for model training than live tick precision.